<title>UK: ABF gains after Geoerge Weston payout.</title>
<headline>ABF gains after Geoerge Weston payout.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-12-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in Associated British Foods Plc rose to a record high on Tuesday after the company's 78 percent-owned Australian unit George Weston Foods announced a surprise A$1 special dividend.</p>
<p>The stock was up 8-1/2p at 454 by 0952 GMT in modest volume of 298,230 shares.</p>
<p>Traders pointed out that ABF has a regular annual shareholders meeting scheduled for Friday and said the George Weston payout could have prompted hopes for a similar move here.</p>
<p>A spokeswoman for ABF declined comment.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom, +44 171 542 5106</p>
